# Test: a daemon that STARTS with a config stamped by a release from before the
# `unmatched` default became discard, holding `vpn ipsec` and no `unmatched` leaf,
# keeps the bypass catch-all that config ran with.
# Config: stamped `# ze-schema: 26.10.01`, vpn ipsec with one leaf,
#         cookie-threshold, the same block ipsec-unmatched-default-discard-said-at-start
#         starts unstamped and gets the discard default.
# Expected: the schema evolution ipsec-unmatched-keeps-bypass runs and says so at
#           the default log level (hub.evolve is left at its default, Warn),
#           naming the command that restores the discard and that the file was
#           saved back; the engine configures, and the start log never says the
#           DISCARD is in force.
#
# VALIDATES: unmatchedBypassEvolution (internal/component/ike/ipsec/unmatched_evolution.go)
#            reached through the real start: the harness writes the config to
#            a file and runs `ze start <file>`, then the hub's schema
#            evolution (applyEvolutions, cmd/ze/hub/main_evolve.go), then the ike
#            plugin's first apply (applyConfig, applyStartup), which would call
#            warnImplicitDiscardAtStart on an unset leaf.
# PREVENTS: a router upgraded across the discard default losing its own BGP and
#           SSH at the next start.
#
# The noop dataplane holds the catch-all without CAP_NET_ADMIN
# (internal/component/ike/dataplane/noop.go), so the test runs unprivileged.

option=env:var=ze_test_ike_dataplane:value=noop
option=env:var=ze_test_ike_port:value=$PORT2
option=env:var=ze.log.ike:value=info
option=timeout:value=30s

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
# ze-schema: 26.10.01
vpn {
	ipsec {
		cookie-threshold 5
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=25s

await=stderr:contains=ike engine configured:then=stop
expect=stderr:contains=config evolution changed behavior
expect=stderr:contains=evolution=ipsec-unmatched-keeps-bypass
expect=stderr:contains=set vpn ipsec unmatched discard
expect=stderr:contains=saved: the file now states the change
reject=stderr:contains=the SPD catch-all DISCARD is in force
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
